('c2fd73ef-34a8-59e8-89f7-d4a89a4db5ab'::uuid,'84f5dd93-d2d8-5de7-b21a-e2ff7911517c'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-H \\| Form 3-07 – Essential Functions Inventory and BIA\n\n| **Department / service** | **Essential function / legal basis** | **Service users / minimum level**          | **People / skills / succession** | **Facilities / ICT / records** | **Dependencies / suppliers**                 | **Impact over time / priority**                        | **Recovery strategy / owner**  |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| \\[Office\\]               | \\[Function and authority\\]           | \\[Who depends on service; minimum output\\] | \\[Key posts, alternates\\]        | \\[Site, system, records\\]      | \\[Power, water, telecom, transport, vendor\\] | \\[Life safety, legal, welfare, financial; time bands\\] | \\[Strategy, owner, resources\\] |\n\nInstructions: Department head validates each function. Proposed recovery time and minimum service levels must be justified by BIA evidence and approved by the designated continuity executive; do not use unsupported generic time targets.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-H.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft'),
