('5a05b982-62f2-517e-8b2f-a98c45ce688a'::uuid,'d323303a-0f9e-5c64-93d6-de5b941aebca'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-L \\| Form 3-11 – Corrective Action and Document Revision Register\n\n| **Finding / source**               | **Root cause** | **Corrective action** | **Accountable owner** | **Due date / resources** | **Verification evidence** | **Closure / escalation**     |\n|------------------------------------|----------------|-----------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------|\n| \\[IAT / exercise / event / audit\\] | \\[Cause\\]      | \\[Action\\]            | \\[Office / official\\] | \\[Date / budget\\]        | \\[Record / test\\]         | \\[Closed by / escalated to\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-L.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft'),
('acbcfc51-7773-5635-982e-f08aa8378879'::uuid,'1e6d98b2-b29d-52c9-9f6d-537cf7b2e265'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-M \\| Source and Methodology Register\n\n| **Source**                                                                        | **Verified use in this chapter**                                                                                          | **Status / qualification**                                                                                                                     |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Republic Act No. 10121 (2010), Lawphil / Supreme Court E-Library                  | Statutory LDRRMC and LDRRMO functions; risk assessment, risk information, local risk map, LDRRMP and contingency planning | Official statutory text; apply with current IRR                                                                                                |\n| DHSUD Memorandum Circular No. 2025-004, Enhanced CDRA Policy                      | Policy intent and minimum approach for standardized enhanced CDRA                                                         | DHSUD learning repository confirms policy purpose; obtain signed circular and annexes for exact operative requirements                         |\n| DHSUD CDRA learning repository: 5-Step+ CDRA Process                              | Detailed sequence for CDRA steps and subsequent compilation, CLUP mainstreaming, M&E and communication                    | Official DHSUD training material; apply current technical parameters and prescribed tools                                                      |\n| PHIVOLCS GIS hazard-map download instructions and Hazard Assessment Services      | Source acquisition, product scale/availability caveats and limits of hazard assessment reports                            | Official PHIVOLCS pages; not a substitute for current technical manuals                                                                        |\n| DILG MC No. 2025-035 / Listo si KAP information                                   | Barangay preparedness and planning responsibilities                                                                       | DILG regional publication confirms initiative; use signed circular and current national quality tools                                          |\n| DILG Quality Assessment System / BDRRM plan template                              | Barangay plan review structure and quality assurance                                                                      | Use current official versions; legacy templates are not presumed current                                                                       |\n| OCD/NDRRMC PSCP Guidebook                                                         | Essential functions, BIA and continuity planning                                                                          | Listed in IAT References as project reference; exact edition and original file must be verified before final technical sign-off                |\n| OCD/NDRRMC contingency-planning manual                                            | Hazard scenario and response planning method                                                                              | Exact edition and original file not located in retrieved project materials; obtain from OCD Region VIII and reconcile this SOP before approval |\n| UNDRR Disaster Resilience Scorecard for Cities – Detailed Level Assessment (2017) | Good-practice benchmarks for scenarios, critical asset failure chains, risk-sensitive planning and ecosystem services     | Benchmark only; IAT crosswalk identifies its adapted indicators                                                                                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-M.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft'),
('5e347d74-8336-5a24-9452-e9c89aa769c0'::uuid,'3189595e-e334-59f9-829b-ac4fb4757c40'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-N \\| Glossary of Terms Used in This Chapter\n\nTerms follow RA 10121, the DHSUD CDRA guidance and the definitions used in Chapters 1 and 2. Where an official definition exists, it governs.\n\n**Table 3.12**\n\n*Glossary of Terms*\n\n| **Term**                                    | **Meaning in this Manual**                                                                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Adaptive capacity                           | The ability of people, institutions and systems to adjust to, prepare for and recover from hazard and climate impacts.                                      |\n| BIA (business impact analysis)              | Assessment of how the disruption of an essential function affects people and the City over time; the basis for recovery priorities (Form 3-07).             |\n| CDRA (Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment) | The DHSUD-prescribed assessment that links hazard and climate information to exposure, vulnerability and risk, and to land-use decisions.                   |\n| Contingency plan                            | An approved, hazard-specific plan setting scenario, triggers, roles, resources and reporting before an event (SOP 3-6).                                     |\n| Critical point facility / lifeline          | A facility (hospital, school, EOC) or network (road, power, water, telecommunications) whose failure affects many people or services.                       |\n| Exposure                                    | People, buildings, production areas, facilities and lifelines located where a hazard may occur.                                                             |\n| Failure chain                               | A traced sequence from a hazard through an asset failure to a service disruption and its consequences (SOP 3-4).                                            |\n| Form                                        | The record a step is closed on. In MODE every workflow and protocol step has a form; the Manual''s form where one exists, otherwise the one-tap step record. |\n| MDA (Major Decision Area)                   | A place or issue where CDRA results require a land-use, investment, social-protection or ecosystem decision (Form 3-04).                                    |\n| Modelled potential damage                   | The value of exposed assets that could be damaged under a model''s assumptions; not an observed loss or an annual expected loss.                             |\n| Process owner                               | The office accountable for an SOP producing its result; others are responsible, consulted or informed (Section 18).                                         |\n| Protocol                                    | A step-by-step operational checklist run at the point of action (for example warning dissemination); it records who closed each step and when.              |\n| PSCP (Public Service Continuity Plan)       | The City plan that keeps essential functions running during disruption (SOP 3-7).                                                                           |\n| Risk Information Register                   | The controlled list of risk datasets with source, custodian, date, scale, access class and version (SOP 3-2).                                               |\n| SOP (standard operating procedure)          | The approved, controlled text in the Manual that states what is done, by whom, under what authority and with what records.                                  |\n| Validation status                           | How far information has been checked: reported, preliminary, field-verified or official (Geo-COP layers; IAT evidence).                                     |\n| Workflow                                    | An SOP made executable in MODE: a sequence of steps across offices over days or weeks, each closed on its form.                                             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-N.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft')
